error[E0270]: `n` of `power` must be known at compile time
  --> comptime_params.ck:13:11
   |
13 |     power n x
   |           ^ this depends on a value only known when the program runs
   = help: pass a literal, a constant, or a `comptime` parameter of the calling function

error[E0271]: `power` is a compile-time function, so it must be called with all its arguments
  --> comptime_params.ck:17:9
   |
17 |     map (power 2) xs
   |         ^^^^^^^^^
   = help: it is expanded where it is called (D59); wrap the call in a lambda to pass it as a value, e.g. `\x -> f 2 x`

error[E0271]: `power` is a compile-time function, so it must be called with all its arguments
  --> comptime_params.ck:20:5
   |
20 |     power
   |     ^^^^^
   = help: it is expanded where it is called (D59); wrap the call in a lambda to pass it as a value, e.g. `\x -> f 2 x`

error[E0272]: a `partial` function can't have `comptime` parameters
  --> comptime_params.ck:27:12
   |
27 | partial fn spin n : n~comptime Nat
   |            ^^^^
   = help: compile-time code must end (D61): only total functions take `comptime` parameters

error[E0272]: a lemma can't have `comptime` parameters
  --> comptime_params.ck:30:7
   |
30 | lemma about n : n~comptime Nat
   |       ^^^^^
   = help: a lemma is never run, so its parameters need no stage; remove `comptime`

